# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ~/Library: a keep-only area. Everything not listed here is skipped, which is
# the point: most of the folder is caches, app containers and developer data
# that can be regenerated. This list is a starting point, edit it to match the
# apps you use. It covers app preferences, keychains, fonts, messages, browser
# and mail data, notes, editor and IDE user settings, and the config files of a
# few apps.
#
# DO NOT put "/Library/" in backup.ignore: an ignore rule wins and stops rsync
# from ever looking inside. Removing every line below has the opposite effect
# and copies the whole folder, because the catch-all disappears with them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/Library/Preferences/
/Library/Keychains/
/Library/Fonts/
/Library/Messages/
/Library/Safari/
/Library/Mail/
/Library/Group Containers/group.com.apple.notes/
/Library/Application Support/Code/User/
/Library/Application Support/Code - Insiders/User/
/Library/Application Support/Cursor/User/
/Library/Application Support/Antigravity/User/
/Library/Application Support/JetBrains/
/Library/Application Support/Signal/
/Library/Application Support/Sublime Text/
/Library/Application Support/Claude/*.json
